RIPE Atlas is the RIPE NCC's global network of probes and anchors that
actively measure Internet connectivity and reachability.  Anyone can
access the measurement data, and probe hosts earn credits to run their
own measurements.

This is the software probe: the probe scripts and the measurement
applets (ping, traceroute, DNS, HTTP, TLS, NTP) that turn a host into a
RIPE Atlas probe once it is registered with the RIPE NCC.
